    "dependencies": [],
    "notes": "The paper primary implementation is VecFalcon. The actual repository API is pre-standard FN-DSA derived from c-fn-dsa, not the original round-3 Falcon API. Empty context and RAW message mode are used; current hash_to_point binds the hashed public key/context unless the legacy 0xFF mode is requested, which is not used here. Signatures are padded fixed-size 666/1280, not compressed variable-size wire format. Exact unpadded statistics parse the compressed polynomial after the 1-byte header and 40-byte nonce, independently checked by comp_decode. Scalar ref disables FNDSA_AVX2 and FNDSA_SSE2 and uses the supported software binary64 implementation; opt AVX2 uses its native SIMD/FPU path. FNDSA_SHAKE256X4=1 matches the artifact Makefile in both. Public C API accepts only encoded keys and exposes no expanded signing state. Native known-answer routines and fixtures are included unchanged through a bench wrapper; only the targeted degree KAT is invoked, avoiding the unrelated large native self-test suite. Important KAT limitation: the opt sampler changes seeded transcripts and its original run_tests comments out test_kat. The inherited full signing-transcript hash KAT fails for opt (first SHA3-256 c677b5dd... vs expected a32f07ba...). The scalar targeted signing KAT is required and passes. For opt, unchanged upstream keygen KATs, original-Falcon verification vectors and its enabled self-tests are required, followed by the fixed-seed cross-build checks. No expected hashes or assertions are modified; this incompatible inherited signing KAT is not reported as a passing test. Revision 2026-11-10: c-fn-dsa is primary and VecFalcon backup. Main ref now uses upstream SSE2 hardware binary64 with AVX2 disabled; it contains SSE2 intrinsics and is not a pure-C portable double path. The source has no FALCON_FPNATIVE switch. Software binary64 is supplemental only. GCC -O3 -march=native plus backend-required options; byte keys, 32-byte messages, fresh key/sign/verify triples, 20 warmup triples and unchanged Dilithium timing files. Every backend pair cross-verifies; equality and first differences are recorded separately. Original local FULL mismatch evidence remains pending until the original vectors are inspected.",
